{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_organisation_config_orgconfig", "label": "Organisation configuration (orgConfig)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four things baked into the code and true of one company: done/inProgress statuses, working week, holidays, sprint length; later trendSprints, countSubtasks, countedTypes, valueFromHierarchy, askField, askFromHierarchy, sizeField."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_config_travels_inside_data", "label": "The config travels inside the data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved once by the producer and written as a top-level orgConfig block; the page, metrics.py, forecast.py, intake.py and the live server all read it there. A config read separately by each consumer is a third opinion by a different route; the first symptom was 25% vs 22% flow efficiency for the same sprint. An emailed copy carries the calendar it was built with."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_inferred_statuses", "label": "Inferred statuses (orgConfig.inferredStatuses)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A status matching no rule falls through to the tracker's category, then a name heuristic, and is recorded and printed. Prevents the quiet failure where a new Awaiting sign-off column reads as To Do and the burndown flattens."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_workflow_chip", "label": "Workflow chip and status mapping control", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lists every status the data mentions with its current meaning and a control to change it. Applying writes into the dataset's own orgConfig.statuses and re-derives every figure; it edits the data, not the view, because a view toggle would have two readers disagreeing from one file and no browser storage to live in."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_two_implementations_one_behaviour", "label": "Two implementations, one behaviour", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "orgconfig.py is the reference; src/app.js mirrors it because the browser cannot call Python. tests/e2e.py asserts agreement under a non-default config since two implementations of Mon-Fri agree by accident. forge/src/jira.js mirrors validate() only, over shared fixtures."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_forge_project_property", "label": "orgConfig Jira project property on Forge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No file to read on Forge, so done statuses come from Jira's own status categories and the working week, holidays and sprint length from a project property named orgConfig, read with a scope the board picker already needs; the app never writes it. When absent the connection label says so."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_bad_config_stops_run", "label": "A bad config stops the run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing is half-applied and nothing falls back; a typo silently reverting to a five-day week would move every forecast with nothing on screen saying so."}, {"id": "docs_organisation_config_units_unchanged", "label": "Holidays affect working days only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Working week and holidays touch the Monte Carlo horizon, elapsed percentage and ideal line; reported elapsed time stays in calendar days. A holiday shortening an item's age would be the same lie as skipping weekends."}, {"id": "agent_tools_orgconfig", "label": "agent/tools/orgconfig.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_orgconfig_from_dataset", "label": "OC.from_dataset()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "forge_src_jira_validate", "label": "jira.validate()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_e2e", "label": "tests/e2e.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_organisation_config_orgconfig", "target": "docs_organisation_config_config_travels_inside_data", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_organisation_config_orgconfig", "target": "docs_organisation_config_inferred_statuses", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/organisation-config.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_organisation_config_inferr